  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gujji drought response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities in Gujji</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drought response in Gujji, Ethiopia</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia is experiencing severe drought impact resulted from the failure of two to three consecutive rainfalls in 2021. The affected regions include the southern pastoral areas of Oromia (especially Borena and Gujji zone), Somali (Afder,Dawa and Liben zones) and SNNP regions. The drought  is a key driver of increased food insecurity in the country. The drought has affected the livelihood of an estimated four million people in the country. Due to the failed rains, water sources and pasture lands are depleted, vegetation conditions are poor, livestock deaths are unusually high (estimated at 170,000-220,000 livestock deaths), food production is declining, and livelihood losses are increasing in the affected regions. In southern part of Oromia for example, 70% of the harvest was lost in 2021.The drought is also displacing communities, as they are forced to find pasture and water for their livestock. In highly affected pastural communities, children drop out of school as families are forced to move with their cattle. Guji Zone is widely affected by climate induced natural hazards and conflict. The Poor performance of last year Ganna/Belg rain and failure of Hagaya/Meher rain has affected the pastoralist districts/woredas and there is serious shortage of pasture, food and water for both human and livestock. A preharvest assessment conducted in 14 woredas by the Zonal Disaster Risk Management and Food Security Office shows that 79% losses in production for highland districts and increased number of livelihood deaths for low-land districts.  The current drought has severely affected nine woredas that are agro-pastoralist.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gujji, Ethiopia</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this project is to save lives, protect livelihoods and promote the early recovery of communities affected by the climate induced drought in Gujji zone. The key interventions include livelihood support through cash assistance, WASH and nutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
